  "id": "COMPOUND:29839 - PROTEIN:5807",
  "verbalization": "Pseudopterosin Q appears to have a direct target relationship with Thioredoxin, mitochondrial, which in turn targets prostate cells through multiple pathways. The evidence suggests that Pseudopterosin Q may act as a modulator of thioredoxin activity, which is involved in various cellular processes, including those relevant to prostate cell function. This mechanism is supported by the presence of multiple targets, including both Yuanhunine and Cyclizidine, which also target prostate cells, indicating a broader role in prostate cell regulation. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential mechanism by which Pseudopterosin Q influences prostate cell behavior, possibly through the modulation of thioredoxin-dependent processes. The evidence supports a role for Pseudopterosin Q in the regulation of prostate cells, though the exact nature of its interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
